{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/426797-sacrificing-a-keshina","id":426797,"title":"Sacrificing a keshina?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-03T12:20:58-08:00","id":426797,"title":"Sacrificing a keshina?","content":"Some seba have powers that are triggered by sacrificing them. In a handful of cases, this is that seba's <i>only</i> power.<br /> <br /> So how do these powers work when the seba in question is bonded to one of the Deceived as a keshina? Does the sacrifice power become a &quot;once per story&quot; ability instead? Does sacrificing supress all of the keshina's powers for a time? Does sacrificing a keshina replace the once-per-Descent &quot;turning back the clock&quot; power of the keshina--that is, if you do one you can't do the other? Are a keshina's sacrifice-triggered powers just unusable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":743,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","user":"Exploding Frogs","date":". 03-03-2015, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T12:41:50-08:00","id":426844,"title":"","content":"I'd use Anointed of the Unseen Ankh (page 5 of Lore of the Deceived) as a model. In other words, it no longer needs to be sacrificed in order to trigger its power, but its power can only be used once per Descent. This has no effect on the other powers specific to Keshina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T15:53:54-08:00","id":427071,"title":"","content":"In general, sacrificing a keshina would mean losing it as a keshina. Yes, that means there are seba that are basically useless as a keshina and make a terrible choice for such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}